Chapter: TreePlanSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Geom
  cites Safari chapter Frame
  cites Safari chapter Trees
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter DepthSort
  cites Safari chapter TreePlan
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 TreePlan: walk the chain, place every tree that survives two culls, and hand the
 survivors to the sort.

 TWO CULLS, AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME REFUSAL. A tree at or behind the near plane
 is not in front of the rider at all; a tree in front but under two pixels tall is
 there and not worth a polygon. They are graded separately, because collapsing
 them into one distance test would pass any check that only counted survivors on
 a normal frame -- the two disagree only at the extremes.

 SCENERY CULLS ON THE LIVE FOCAL AND CRITTERS DO NOT, which the chapter says in
 prose and is the reason the focal is a parameter here. Passing a small focal is
 how the size cull is reached without moving anything: at a focal of 1 a
 five-metre tree six metres away is under two pixels, and the whole segment
 vanishes.

 THE COUNTS COME FROM THE ROUTE. Segment 0 is 500 metres and fills 14 pairs -- 28
 trees from six metres in, every thirty, stopping eighty-five short of the end.
 Moving the rider 100 metres up it puts the first four pairs behind him, which is
 20 survivors, and that arithmetic is the test.

 We say:

Section: The Chain

  segs : List Segment
  segs = [segment-at 0, segment-at 1, segment-at 2]

  chain : List Integer
  chain = [0, 1, 2]

  origin : Pose
  origin = Pose { along = 0.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, hw = 2.0 }

  up-road : Pose
  up-road = Pose { along = 100.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, hw = 2.0 }

  planted-got : List Integer
  planted-got =
    [ list-length (list-at segs 0).trees,
      list-length (list-at segs 1).trees,
      list-length (list-at segs 2).trees,
      max-vis-trees ]

  planted-want : List Integer
  planted-want = [28, 16, 22, 640]

Section: One Tree

 At the origin looking straight down the road, a tree's depth is its along and
 its right is its across -- the half-width shifts it to from-the-left and the
 rider transform shifts it back.

  one : List TreeItem
  one = place-tree segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (Tree { along = 120.0, across = 3.5, color = 1858082, height = 5.85 })

  one-got : List Real
  one-got = [(list-at one 0).right, (list-at one 0).fwd, (list-at one 0).height]

  one-want : List Real
  one-want = [3.5, 120.0, 5.85]

  one-colour-got : List Integer
  one-colour-got = [list-length one, (list-at one 0).color]

  one-colour-want : List Integer
  one-colour-want = [1, 1858082]

 Behind the eye, and under two pixels. Neither survives, and the second is in
 front of the rider when it goes.

  cull-got : List Integer
  cull-got =
    [ list-length (place-tree segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (Tree { along = 0.4, across = 3.5, color = 1858082, height = 5.85 })),
      list-length (place-tree segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (Tree { along = 0.5, across = 3.5, color = 1858082, height = 5.85 })),
      list-length (place-tree segs chain origin 0 1.0 2.0 (Tree { along = 120.0, across = 3.5, color = 1858082, height = 5.85 })),
      list-length (place-tree segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (Tree { along = 2000.0, across = 3.5, color = 1858082, height = 5.85 })) ]

  cull-want : List Integer
  cull-want = [0, 1, 0, 0]

Section: The Walk

 Every tree on every segment of the chain, in chain order. At the origin all of
 segment 0's survive; a hundred metres up the road the first four pairs are
 behind the rider.

  seg0-got : List Integer
  seg0-got =
    [ list-length (seg-trees segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (list-at segs 0).trees 0),
      list-length (seg-trees segs chain up-road 0 500.0 2.0 (list-at segs 0).trees 0),
      list-length (seg-trees segs chain origin 0 1.0 2.0 (list-at segs 0).trees 0) ]

  seg0-want : List Integer
  seg0-want = [28, 20, 0]

 The trees come out in the order they were planted, so the first pair is the
 nearest and they straddle the road.

  order-got : List Real
  order-got =
    let ts = seg-trees segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (list-at segs 0).trees 0
    in [ (list-at ts 0).fwd, (list-at ts 1).fwd, (list-at ts 2).fwd,
         (list-at ts 0).right, (list-at ts 1).right ]

  order-want : List Real
  order-want = [6.0, 6.0, 36.0, -3.5, 3.5]

 Alternate pairs are the taller tree, which is the tier scheme's doing rather
 than anything TreePlan decides -- and 4.5 * 1.3 is not the literal 5.85, so this
 line carries a tolerance where the hand-built tree above did not.

  height-got : List Real
  height-got =
    let ts = seg-trees segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (list-at segs 0).trees 0
    in [(list-at ts 0).height, (list-at ts 2).height]

  height-want : List Real
  height-want = [5.85, 4.5]

Section: Into the Frame

 One item per surviving tree, indexed by its place in the collected list, so the
 sort can find it again.

  items-got : List Integer
  items-got =
    let ts = seg-trees segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (list-at segs 0).trees 0
    in let its = tree-items ts 0
    in [ list-length its, (list-at its 0).i, (list-at its 27).i, list-length (tree-items [] 0) ]

  items-want : List Integer
  items-want = [28, 0, 27, 0]

  item-fwd-got : List Real
  item-fwd-got =
    let its = tree-items (seg-trees segs chain origin 0 500.0 2.0 (list-at segs 0).trees 0) 0
    in [(list-at its 0).fwd, (list-at its 2).fwd]

  item-fwd-want : List Real
  item-fwd-want = [6.0, 36.0]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "te-plant " planted-got planted-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "te-one   " one-got one-want 0.0001)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "te-colour" one-colour-got one-colour-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "te-cull  " cull-got cull-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "te-seg0  " seg0-got seg0-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "te-order " order-got order-want 0.0001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "te-height" height-got height-want 0.000000000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "te-items " items-got items-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "te-ifwd  " item-fwd-got item-fwd-want 0.0001)
  end
